        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1164"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Daggett.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5,
                        1883</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon the receipt of your No. 63 of the 6th
                    ultimo I promptly communicated to the Secretary of the Navy your request
                    touching the presence of a war vessel in the Hawaiian Islands. I have now
                    received Mr. Chandler’s reply, of the 3d instant, in which he states that
                    although his Department will be unable to keep a ship constantly at Honolulu, he
                    has given such directions as will insure one of its vessels visiting that port
                    at as frequent intervals as practicable.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred’k T.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
